QUESTION [a7fff9314130]: What is the capital of Australia, and why is it not Sydney?

Seat weights from memory (before this run): atlas=1.60, vega=1.38, orion=1.52

  [atlas] answer C via openrouter:dots-studio/dots-3-note-preview:free (22.7s)  critic score: 10.0/10
     The capital of Australia is Canberra. Although Sydney is the country's largest city and a major economic hub, the capital was not Sydney. In 1908, after a dispute between Sydney and Melbourne, the federal government chose a site inland, creating the Australian Capital Territory, to serve as a neutral administrative centre.
     sources: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canberra, https://www.britannica.com/place/Canberra, https://www.australia.gov.au/about-australia/our-country
  [vega] answer B via openrouter:nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free (15.0s)  critic score: 10.0/10
     The capital of Australia is Canberra, not Sydney. When the Commonwealth was federated in 1901, Sydney and Melbourne rivaled each other for the capital. As compromise, the Constitution mandated a new capital in New South Wales, at least 100 miles from Sydney. Canberra was selected in 1908, officially founded in 1913, purpose-built to seat government and break the deadlock between the two largest cities.
     sources: https://www.britannica.com/place/Canberra-capital-of-Australia, https://www.nca.gov.au/about-canberra/history, https://www.aph.gov.au/About_Parliament/Parliamentary_departments/Parliamentary_Library/FlagPost/Canberra_the_capital_of_Australia
  [orion] answer A via openrouter:recursive/flint-v1.0:free (16.9s)  critic score: 10.0/10
     The capital is Canberra, not Sydney. The common misconception is to name Sydney because it's Australia's largest city and iconic. The real reason is political: when federation created the Commonwealth in 1901, Sydney and Melbourne competed as rivals. The Constitution therefore picked a compromise capital, Canberra, in New South Wales but away from Sydney, and it became the seat of government. So Sydney is the biggest
     sources: https://www.aph.gov.au/, https://www.legislation.gov.au/, https://www.canberra.gov.au/

